My strongest recommendation

Don’t make the dashboards static.

Create a Widget Marketplace within SKULOS where users (based on permissions) can:

* Add widgets
* Remove widgets
* Rearrange widgets with drag-and-drop
* Collapse or expand sections
* Save multiple dashboard layouts
* Reset to default

For example, a Principal may want “Academic Performance” at the top, while another prefers “Revenue” and “Attendance.” By making dashboards customizable, SKULOS becomes more personal and powerful, giving each user a workspace tailored to how they manage their responsibilities. This is a feature found in premium enterprise platforms and would be a strong differentiator for SKULOS.
